{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And now, send your livestock.</b> And if you will say: if so, what does this plague accomplish? Behold, you have before you what HaShem prefaced by saying to him — that the purpose of the plagues is not to do harm, but rather in order to show him His great power and His strong hand. And therefore He informed him that he should gather man and beast from the field. In any case, the plague will make an impression of destruction upon whatever is attached to the earth, as it is written: ״וְאֵת כָּל עֵשֶׂב הַשָּׂדֶה הִכָּה הַבָּרָד וְאֶת כָּל עֵץ הַשָּׂדֶה שִׁבֵּר״ (Exodus 9:25)." "<b>There remains</b> for us to discern in the word <b>ועתה</b> what our God on high intends by it. If we take it literally as its plain sense — at that time, why would the El command about this, since the hail does not fall until tomorrow at that hour? Or perhaps it is because this amount of time is needed to send word to the place where man and beast are, and to return and gather them home." "<b>Further,</b> it appears that we should preface with a question: the word of HaShem, ״שְׁלַח הָעֵז״ — toward whom does it incline? If toward one who fears the word of HaShem, he on his own, when he hears that tomorrow HaShem will rain hail on the field, will fear and bring in his servants and his livestock. Rather, it is certain that the words came only to one who does not fear the word of HaShem. Accordingly, the intention in saying <b>ועתה</b> is according to the statement of the Sages of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 51; Midrash Tehillim 100:2): ״ועתה״ means nothing other than repentance. For since they do not set the word of HaShem upon their heart, therefore He said to them that they should return in repentance and set the word of HaShem upon their heart, that it will indeed be done, and bring in from the field, etc. And Scripture informs that the wicked did not return in repentance and did not set their heart, etc., and the fire of HaShem burned among them."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {2 "The source citations Genesis Rabbah 51 and Midrash Tehillim 100:2 are rendered as they appear in the Hebrew text; the chapter/section numbers follow the standard printed editions referenced."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:16.277910411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}